# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# Text files are stored LF in the repository and checked out LF on every
# OS and git client. Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by
# default) rewrites the tree to CRLF on checkout, so a subsequent WSL or
# Linux git -- which leaves core.autocrlf unset -- reports every file as
# modified even on a fresh clone. eol=lf forces the working-tree ending;
# text=auto lets git auto-detect binary files and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
